 "remarks": "Welcome to 14 Park Lane in Harborview, located in one of Norwalk's most coveted private associations. This charming 1930s coastal colonial blends classic character with updated living, set within a private Beach Association on Long Island Sound. This close-knit neighborhood dates back to 1904 and offers a fully equipped clubhouse, docks, moorings, two har-tru tennis courts, a ball field, and a playground. Inside, enjoy a light-filled, open layout. The first floor features a spacious living room flowing into an eat-in kitchen and family room, plus a private office tucked behind French doors. Upstairs, the primary suite includes an updated en-suite bath and a large walk-in closet. The two additional bedrooms share a full bath. Outside, a dry, private lot offers a flat backyard and a cozy deck with plenty of room for dining and lounging. Importantly, 14 Park Lane sits up high and has never had a FEMA claim. Nearly everything in this tasteful home has been touched; don't miss your opportunity to own a turnkey home in the most beautiful beach community.",
